'''[[Thomas Mundy Peterson]]''' (October 6, 1824 – February 4, 1904) was a resident of [[Perth Amboy, New Jersey]], who has been claimed to be the first [[African Americans|African American]] to vote in an election under the provisions of the [[Fifteenth Amendment to the United States Constitution|15th Amendment]] to the [[Constitution of the United States]]. His vote was cast on March 31, 1870; the Amendment had been ratified almost two months earlier, on February 3, but was only officially certified by Secretary of State [[Hamilton Fish]] on March 30. To honor him as the first African-American voter after the passage of the 15th Amendment, in 1884, the citizens of Perth Amboy raised $70 (${{<!--
